# Sample config for amiga_sample_convert wrappers.
#
# Copy this to ~/.config/amiga_sample_convert/config and edit the values.
# It's sourced by the upload wrappers via `source`, so it's plain zsh.
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/amiga_sample_convert
#   cp /path/to/repo/macos/config.sample ~/.config/amiga_sample_convert/config
#
# All keys are optional — anything you don't set falls back to the wrapper's
# built-in defaults.

# Where to upload converted .iff files. Full smb:// URL with optional
# user@ and any subpath inside the share. The wrapper auto-mounts and
# auto-creates the target subdirectory.
#
# Default: smb://mister/sdcard/games/Amiga/shared/samples
#
# AMIGA_SMB_URL="smb://mister/sdcard/games/Amiga/shared/samples"

# Extra flags to pass to amiga_sample_convert.sh on every run. Useful if
# you want all your uploaded samples to share a particular treatment
# (e.g. always normalize, always trim silence). The -P24 sibling wrapper
# overrides this with -P 24 regardless of what you set here.
#
# AMIGA_CONVERT_FLAGS="-n -t"
